# H3 quartet, bending the linear chain: bond d = 0.22 (Nader R_eq), angle alpha = H-H-H in the x-z plane,
# central atom on the B axis before centring; alpha = 180 linear along B (file 15), alpha = 60 the x90 triangle.
# Two starts per angle (mol: Lz 0, -1, -2; atm: three translated 1s); the lower E_phys counts.
# Summary: bash summarize.sh results/18_H3_bent_B425 <3 E(H) from file 10>
COMMON B=425.5 k=10 thresh=1e-6 eprec=1e-9 L=8 qextra=10 h=0.25 tmin=1e-8 tmax_factor=45 dphi=3 inner=3 tolscf=1e-5 rcut=1.0 rtaper=0.1 maxscf=40
alpha180_mol  nelec=3 state=highspin axial=1 mlist=0,-1,-2 E0list=203,207,209 "atoms=1,0,0,-0.22;1,0,0,0;1,0,0,0.22"
alpha180_atm  nelec=3 state=highspin axial=0 mloc=0 E0=207 "atoms=1,0,0,-0.22;1,0,0,0;1,0,0,0.22"
